{%- doc -%}
  The trail above a page's title (Figma: Standart Product Page → "Home / Gift
  Boxes / We Miss You Deluxe Gift Box").

  `links` takes anything with `.title` and `.url`, which is the shape a collection,
  a page, a blog and an article already have — so a caller hands over the resources
  it has rather than assembling a list of hashes Liquid makes awkward to build.
  Home is the snippet's own and is not passed in.

  The current page is the last item and carries no link: a link to where you
  already are is a control that does nothing. It is marked `aria-current="page"`
  so the trail still reads as a position rather than as four loose words.

  A caller that has words rather than a resource — a collection page whose parent is
  a nav item, not another collection — hands over `parent_title` and `parent_url`
  instead. That step is drawn after `links`, and it exists because building a
  one-item list of hashes is the thing Liquid makes awkward.

  @param {object[]} [links] - The steps between home and the current page.
  @param {string} [parent_title] - A single step written out, drawn after `links`.
  @param {string} [parent_url] - Where that step goes. Without it the step is dropped.
  @param {string} current - The current page's title.
  @param {string} [home_label] - The first step's wording. Defaults to "Home".
  @param {string} [class] - Additional CSS classes.

  @example
  {% render 'ui-breadcrumb', links: product.collections, current: product.title %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  # Plain English rather than a `t:` key: locales/*.json carries no breadcrumb
  # wording, and docs/section-settings.md rules out inventing one.
  assign crumb_home = home_label | default: 'Home'
-%}

<nav class="ui-breadcrumb{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol class="ui-breadcrumb__list">
    <li class="ui-breadcrumb__item">
      <a class="ui-breadcrumb__link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ crumb_home }}</a>
    </li>
    {%- for link in links -%}
      {%- if link.title == blank or link.url == blank -%}{% continue %}{%- endif -%}
      <li class="ui-breadcrumb__item">
        <a class="ui-breadcrumb__link" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if parent_title != blank and parent_url != blank -%}
      <li class="ui-breadcrumb__item">
        <a class="ui-breadcrumb__link" href="{{ parent_url }}">{{ parent_title }}</a>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if current != blank -%}
      <li class="ui-breadcrumb__item">
        <span class="ui-breadcrumb__current" aria-current="page">{{ current }}</span>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}
  </ol>
</nav>

{% stylesheet %}
  .ui-breadcrumb {
    color: var(--ui-color-gray);
    font-family: var(--ui-font-body);
    font-size: var(--ui-breadcrumb-font-size, 14px);
    font-weight: var(--ui-font-body-weight);
    line-height: var(--ui-line-height);
  }

  .ui-breadcrumb__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    /* Column gap only: a trail that wraps should not open a gap between its lines. */
    column-gap: 4px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  /*
   * The separator is generated rather than written into the markup, so a screen
   * reader is not read a slash between every step and the trail can wrap on it.
   */
  .ui-breadcrumb__item + .ui-breadcrumb__item::before {
    content: '/';
    margin-inline-end: 4px;
    color: var(--ui-color-gray);
  }

  .ui-breadcrumb__link {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .ui-breadcrumb__link:hover {
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .ui-breadcrumb__current {
    color: var(--ui-color-black);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
